{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_21","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"c2rust transpile --help | sed -n '1,240p'\"","aggregated_output":"transpile 0.22.1\n- The C2Rust Project Developers <c2rust@immunant.com>\n- Eric Mertens <emertens@galois.com>\n- Alec Theriault <atheriault@galois.com>\nTranslate C code to equivalent Rust code\n\nUSAGE:\n    c2rust-transpile [OPTIONS] [COMPILE_COMMANDS]... [-- <EXTRA_CLANG_ARGS>...]\n\nARGS:\n    <COMPILE_COMMANDS>...    Path to compile_commands.json, or a list of source files\n    <EXTRA_CLANG_ARGS>...    Extra arguments to pass to clang frontend during parsing the input\n                             C file\n\nOPTIONS:\n    -b, --binary <BINARY>\n            Emit Rust build files for a binary using the main function in the specified translation\n            unit (implies -e/--emit-build-files)\n\n        --c2rust-dir <C2RUST_DIR>\n            If building from the c2rust repo, the path to it. This is needed to use relative paths\n            for up-to-date dependencies (as opposed to what is published on crates.io)\n\n        --cross-check-backend <CROSS_CHECK_BACKEND>\n            [default: zstd-logging] [possible values: dynamic-dlsym, zstd-logging, libclevrbuf-sys,\n            libfakechecks-sys]\n\n        --ddebug-labels\n            Generate readable 'current_block' values in relooper\n\n        --ddump-cfgs-liveness\n            Dump into the DOT file visualizations liveness information\n\n        --ddump-function-cfgs\n            Dumps into files DOT visualizations of the CFGs of every function\n\n        --ddump-structures\n            Dumps out to STDERR the intermediate structures produced by relooper\n\n        --debug-ast-exporter\n            Debug Clang AST exporter plugin\n\n        --disable-refactoring\n            Disable running refactoring tool after translation\n\n        --disable-rustfmt\n            Disable running rustfmt after translation\n\n        --dump-typed-clang-ast\n            Prints out the parsed typed Clang AST\n\n        --dump-untyped-clang-ast\n            Prints out CBOR based Clang AST\n\n    -e, --emit-build-files\n            Emit Rust build files, i.e., Cargo.toml for a library (and one or more binaries if\n            -b/--binary is given). Implies --emit-modules\n\n        --emit-c-decl-map\n            Write map of C decls corresponding to each translated Rust item alongside the transpiled\n            output with the extension `.c_decls.json`\n\n        --emit-modules\n            Emit .rs files as modules instead of crates, excluding the crate preambles\n\n        --emit-no-std\n            Emit code using core rather than std\n\n    -f, --filter <FILTER>\n            Only transpile files matching filter\n\n        --fail-on-error\n            Fail to translate a module when a portion is not able to be translated\n\n        --fail-on-multiple\n            Fail when the control-flow graph generates branching constructs\n\n    -h, --help\n            Print help information\n\n        --ignore-c-loop-info\n            Don't keep/use information about C loops\n\n        --ignore-c-multiple-info\n            Don't keep/use information about C branches\n\n        --invalid-code <INVALID_CODE>\n            How to handle violated invariants or invalid code [default: compile_error] [possible\n            values: panic, compile_error]\n\n        --json-function-cfgs\n            Dumps into files JSON visualizations of the CFGs of every function\n\n        --log-level <LOG_LEVEL>\n            Logging level [default: WARN]\n\n        --no-incremental-relooper\n            Disable relooping function bodies incrementally\n\n        --no-simplify-structures\n            Do not run a pass to simplify structures\n\n    -o, --output-dir <DIR>\n            Path to output directory. Rust sources will be emitted in DIR/src/ and build files will\n            be emitted in DIR/\n\n        --overwrite-existing\n            Emit files 